<p>Dear Tom,</p>
<p>Further to our meeting last week, please find attached Schedule 7
(Limitation of Liability) for the maintenance contract covering the pumping
and cooling plant at our two data centres.</p>
<p>As a PRA-regulated firm, we have to meet our regulators' expectations on
outsourcing and third-party risk. The schedule therefore includes a higher
cap for data breach (three times the annual charges) and makes the supplier
liable without limit for regulatory fines that result from the supplier's
default. These are standard requirements for our material suppliers.</p>
<p>We need your comments by Wednesday 4 November, so that the contract can
go to our supplier risk committee on 11 November.</p>
<p>Kind regards</p>
<p>Olivia Grant<br>
